{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119757","id":3744100918,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7fKnI2","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119757","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119757.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119757.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119757","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119757/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119757/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119757/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/374102cfbeedbed3d17833d22f258939cef9c6f7","number":119757,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix `ResourceLoader::load_threaded_get()` deadlocks","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This fixes several issues in ResourceLoader\r\n\r\n* When waiting on resources being loaded on the main thread it is possible that the resource was waiting on the message queue. Flush the message queue in this situation. This was an existing bug. \r\n* When re-starting a load for deadlock-prevention reasons, and this type of resource has nested resources and uses resource changed connections we end up with references to resourcese being deleted as duplicates in the dependent task. We now keep a reference to these resources for the duration of the dependent load task. This closes the race but does not entirely eliminate it during intial import.  This is an existing bug seemingly specific to TileSetSource but there might be others.\r\n* When threads are waiting during teardown we ended up deadlocking because the waiting thread would never end up completing. This is a bug introduced by f63ab5f\r\n* When a thread loading a resource ends up calling back into the WorkerThreadPool to wait cooperatively it expects that other threads complete, or new requests are made, so that work moves forward. If all OTHER threads end up blocked by the WorkerThreadPool waiting thread then no forward progress can be made anymore. We now solve this problem by yielding whenever we are blocked by another task. We wake up each every task whenever any progress is made to see if further progress can be made. This is a bug introduced by f63ab5f \r\n* When dependencies get introduced while loading it is possible to form a dependency cycle. Normally this isn't a problem but when all threads are already waiting when the cycle is introduced no forward progress can be made anymore. We now break such cycles. This is a bug introduced by f63ab5f\r\n \r\nTesting was done on the reproduction cases for\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118824 \r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115069\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111202\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115069\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98865\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/84012\r\n* the project provided by max in private. \r\n\r\nAdditionally the various tests were performed with the default thread pool size, 1,2,8,16 and 1024 threads. No deadlocks or memory corruptions were found.\r\n\r\nFurther testing was done by making all ERR_ macros fatal (always generating a trap) and running the various MRPs in tight loops. This did uncover some issues in the Dummy display server, but these turned out to also exist in master. \r\n\r\nI believe this now fixes all known issues with f63ab5f\r\n\r\nNote that for #115069 specifically this addresses the *crash*, there is still an unrelated `TileSetSource` issue causing the tileset in the MRP to occasionally not show up. This will have to be addressed in a different PR.\r\n\r\nFor #98865 the reported error no longer appears, but that seems incidental. The problem is that loading a GDScript resource the `GDScriptAnalyzer` wants to refer to Nodes being processed on a different WorkerThread, which it then can't.\r\n\r\nFor #84012 it seems that the crashes are bad loads are much reduced, but there is much message spam like for #98865, it appears to be the same issue. The problem here appears to be `SCRIPT ERROR: Parse Error: Could not find type \"InteractableObject\" in the current scope.` which seems to indicate that some dependency is not being recorded properly. Given the age of this report I think that this can't be a regression.\r\n\r\n(For people following along all of the tests have been re-ran)\r\n(EDIT 28/05/2026: test have been re-ran again with more MRPs and with DEV_ASSERTS enabled, but not with various thread pool sizes again.)","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","de